   Lean-target only; OCaml output byte-identical. The are_compatible
   mutual family recurses through ctype subterms carried in pairs and
   pair-lists — beyond Lean's automatic termination derivation (the
   arc-3 pair-list finding, see core_run_aux.lem): fuel, all-or-none
   across the mutual block (backend requirement). lemDefaultFuel (10^6)
   dominates any real ctype depth by orders of magnitude; exhaustion is
   LOUD (fuelExhausted panics — fail-closed, never a silent default).
   Ruling [USER, V2 close 2026-08-28]: the model is to be made total
   properly; signed off as lem-side fuel. === -/

/- FUEL MEASURE (fuel-parameter arc C3, 2026-09-05; Lean-only): the block shares ONE
   fuel counter, so each member's measure bounds the WHOLE block's call depth from
   that entry. are_compatible: the two ctypes' derived sizes. are_compatible_params_aux:
   its recursion argument is the `function` scrutinee (hoisted as `lemTail` since lem
   d4ba548), a PAIR of parameter lists whose element ctypes are recursed into by
   are_compatible — the measure is the derived size of both lists (`ctype_.lemSize_aux1`,
   the backend's helper for `list (qualifiers * ctype * bool)`; `List.length` alone is
   not sufficient). are_compatible_params calls the aux at fuel - 1 on the same lists,
   hence its + 2. Proved in lean_frontend/AilTypesAux_lemMeasureProofs.lean. -/
